      "role": "user",
      "content": "The dialogue feels a bit stilted and the phrasing is a little off for Alabama in the 50s. Let's try to make it more visceral. I want the tension to be palpable. \n\nCan you rewrite this scene? I want the conversation to get deeper into their actual attitudes. Instead of being vague about \"the market,\" have them talk more explicitly about how they feel about the changing social order. They're worried about their status and their businesses being \"tainted\" or losing their traditional way of life. Make the dialogue sound like two men actually talking in a smoke-filled room back then—bitter, maybe a bit more blunt about the racial hierarchy they're used to.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
